== Match report ==

=== Nusaraya 2–1 Jacan ===
[[Nusaraya national football team|Nusaraya]] claimed the runner-up spot in Group G with a hard-fought win over [[Jacan national football team|Jacan]] in [[Castramara]]. [[Bagas Prasetyo]] opened the scoring in the 33rd minute, but Jacan equalised through a second-half strike. [[Dimas Saputra]] struck in the 84th minute to seal all three points and send Nusaraya through.

=== United Midlands 2–1 Yanbaru ===
[[United Midlands national football team|United Midlands]] secured top spot in Group H with a 2–1 win over [[Yanbaru national football team|Yanbaru]] in [[Sanropura]]. [[Oliver Hartley]] gave the home side the lead in the 23rd minute, and [[Samuel Wren]] doubled the advantage in the 70th. Yanbaru pulled one back three minutes later but couldn't find an equaliser.

=== Daras 0–1 Sinchew ===
[[Sinchew national football team|Sinchew]] stunned [[Daras national football team|Daras]] in [[Uxiu]], snatching a late winner in the 70th minute to claim the runner-up spot in Group I and eliminate Daras.

=== Pangkajene 2–1 Breisland ===
[[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] advanced as Group J runners-up with a dramatic late win over [[Breisland national football team|Breisland]] in [[Telukuba]]. Breisland took the lead in the 39th minute, but [[Andi Akbar]] equalised in the 59th before [[Muhammad Asri]] scored a stoppage-time winner in the 90+3rd minute.

=== Sarta 0–1 Potocsí ===
[[Potocsí national football team|Potocsí]] pulled off an upset in [[Pangkalsimpang]], scoring early through a 6th-minute goal and holding on to claim the runner-up spot in Group K and eliminate [[Sarta national football team|Sarta]].

=== Louyang 0–2 Louyan ===
[[Louyan national football team|Louyan]] pulled off a shock win over [[Louyang national football team|Louyang]] in [[Yerba Buena]], scoring in the 66th minute and adding a second in stoppage time to claim the runner-up spot in Group L.

== Summary ==

Matchday 6 produced 11 goals and completed the group stage. [[United Midlands national football team|United Midlands]], [[Nusaraya national football team|Nusaraya]], [[Sinchew national football team|Sinchew]], [[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]], [[Potocsí national football team|Potocsí]], and [[Louyan national football team|Louyan]] all secured the wins they needed to advance to the knockout stage.

